<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLAND V AUSTRALIA FOURTH TEST SCOREBOARD.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLAND V AUSTRALIA FOURTH TEST SCOREBOARD.</headline>
<dateline>LEEDS, England 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scoreboard on the final</p>
<p>day of the fourth test between England and Australia at</p>
<p>Headingley on Monday:</p>
<p>England first innings 172 (J.Gillespie 7-37)</p>
<p>Australia first innings 501-9 declared (M.Elliott 199,</p>
<p>R.Ponting 127, P.Reiffel 54 not out; D.Gough 5-149)</p>
<p>England second innings (overnight 212-4)</p>
<p> M.Butcher c Healy b McGrath	 19</p>
<p> M.Atherton c Warne b McGrath	 2</p>
<p> A.Stewart b Reiffel		   16</p>
<p> N.Hussain c Gillespie b Warne    105</p>
<p> G.Thorpe c M.Waugh b Gillespie    15</p>
<p> J.Crawley b Reiffel		   72</p>
<p> M.Ealham c M.Waugh b Reiffel	 4</p>
<p> D.Headley lbw b Reiffel		3</p>
<p> R.Croft c Healy b Reiffel	    5</p>
<p> D.Gough c M.Waugh b Gillespie	0</p>
<p> M.Smith not out			  4</p>
<p> Extras (b-6 lb-4 nb-13)	     23</p>
<p> Total				    268</p>
<p>Fall of wickets: 1-23 2-28 3-57 4-89 5-222 6-252</p>
<p>7-256 8-263 9-264</p>
<p>Bowling: McGrath 22-5-80-2, Reiffel 21.1-2-49-5, Gillespie</p>
<p>23-8-65-2, Warne 21-6-53-1, S.Waugh 4-1-11-0</p>
<p>Result: Australia won by an innings and 61 runs</p>
<p>First test: Edgbaston - England won by 9 wickets</p>
<p>Second test: Lord's - Match drawn</p>
<p>Third test: Old Trafford - Australia won by 268 runs</p>
<p>Fifth test: Trent Bridge - August 7 to 11</p>
<p>Sixth test: The Oval - August 21-25</p>
</text>
